verify_rubric.description:
Rubric for verify_enabled: {"dimensions": ["groundedness", "completeness", "accuracy"], "hard_gate": …, "max_attempts": …,
"scorer": …, "dimension_defs": {…}}. Add "evidence": true or {"dimensions": [...], "required_tools": ["send_report"], "max_chars": 1500}
to let the scorer also see which tools completed or failed in that turn (no argument values or results; same number of calls).

clear_fields.description:
Fields to empty — empty values are otherwise ignored. Allowed: description;
args, env_vars_schema, cli_args_mapping (removed from the stored local config, the rest is kept);
env_vars, auth_config (both are the one stored credentials object — clearing either removes
all stored credentials). The result lists them under "cleared".

tools.description:
Check a run started with start_run (or any session of yours) and read its answer when done.

Returns the platform's processing fields plus "status":
  "running"   — still working (current_agent, elapsed_seconds tell you where it is); poll again;
  "completed" — the newest turn is an assistant reply; "result" holds it (include_result=True);
  "timed_out" — the platform stopped it after 120 minutes;
  "pending"   — the session exists but nothing has been said yet; poll again;
  "no_reply"  — not running, and the newest message is the user's: the run ended without an answer;
  "not_found" — no such session for this key (wrong id, or another user's session).
Right after start_run on a session that already had turns, the previous answer can show as
"completed" until the new run begins — trust "completed" once you have seen "running".

schedule_config.description:
REQUIRED — the backend rejects the request with 400 when it is missing, so the
"daily" default above is not usable on its own. Times are KST. Shape per type:
daily: {"time": "09:00"}
weekly: {"time": "09:00", "weekdays": [0,1,2,3,4]}  (0=Monday)
monthly: {"day": 1, "time": "09:00"}
every_minutes: {"interval": 30}
every_hours: {"interval": 6}
once: {"run_at": "2025-12-01T09:00:00"}

changes.description:
Ordered list of change dicts. Each must have "action" key. Action schemas:
create_agent: {"action": "create_agent", "agent": {name, agent_type, instruction, model, tools, ...}}
    - tools is a list of strings: ["tool_name1", "tool_name2"]
update_agent: {"action": "update_agent", "agent_id": "...", "agent": {only the fields to change}}
delete_agent: {"action": "delete_agent", "agent_id": "..."}
update_orchestrator: {"action": "update_orchestrator", "changes": {instruction, model, tools, sub_agents: [agent_id, ...]}}
    - sub_agents are linked to the orchestrator automatically
add_sub_agent: {"action": "add_sub_agent", "base_agent_id": "...", "sub_agent_id": "...", "order_index": 1}
remove_sub_agent: {"action": "remove_sub_agent", "base_agent_id": "...", "sub_agent_id": "..."}
link_mcp: {"action": "link_mcp", "agent_id": "...", "platform_id": "..."}
unlink_mcp: {"action": "unlink_mcp", "agent_id": "...", "platform_id": "..."}
link_composio: {"action": "link_composio", "agent_id": "...", "auth_config_id": "...", "enabled_tools": ["GMAIL_SEND_EMAIL"]}
    - "enabled_tools" is optional: exact names from list_composio_integration_tools; left out = the app's whole toolkit.
      It is saved only when the link is new — change an existing link with set_agent_enabled_tools
unlink_composio: {"action": "unlink_composio", "agent_id": "...", "auth_config_id": "..."}
link_device: {"action": "link_device", "agent_id": "...", "device_id": "..."}
unlink_device: {"action": "unlink_device", "agent_id": "...", "device_id": "..."}
(add_sub_agent / remove_sub_agent also accept parent_agent_id / child_agent_id.)
